WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:04.789
Reserve helps coaches prepare a whole global Hard Fearless series.

00:00:04.809 --> 00:00:10.343
This is a fictional practice plan: Ember and Tide are tied one to one before Game three.

00:00:10.363 --> 00:00:16.362
The board covers all ten players through Games 3, 4, and 5: 30 remaining slots.

00:00:18.362 --> 00:00:20.716
Compare Tide's support choices.

00:00:20.736 --> 00:00:23.429
Rell fills 29 of 30 slots.

00:00:23.449 --> 00:00:27.261
Three Ember support turns share just Alistar and Braum.

00:00:27.281 --> 00:00:29.200
Thresh fills all 30.

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:32.640
Each board is one allocation witness for these pools.

00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:35.570
Gameplay and tactical choices stay with the coach.

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:40.014
Use your own permitted CSV.

00:00:40.034 --> 00:00:48.216
Here I import the bundled fictional observations, set an explicit UTC cutoff, and inspect distinct earlier game counts.

00:00:48.236 --> 00:00:51.725
Propose from observations marks the pool for review.

00:00:51.745 --> 00:00:55.330
I check the assigned support role and confirm the playable pool.

00:00:57.330 --> 00:01:00.828
Earlier picks consume the shared reserve across games.

00:01:00.848 --> 00:01:07.838
Watch a current Rell ban: on Base preparation, Rell leaves Game three and remains available for a future game.

00:01:07.858 --> 00:01:11.442
I undo this temporary ban before choosing a support pick.

00:01:13.442 --> 00:01:17.428
Selecting a comparison leaves the actual draft unchanged.

00:01:17.448 --> 00:01:20.955
I compare Thresh, then lock it for Tide's support.

00:01:20.975 --> 00:01:26.450
That current pick consumes Thresh elsewhere while the plan still fills all thirty remaining slots.

00:01:28.450 --> 00:01:32.211
Save JSON preserves the complete preparation and evidence.

00:01:32.231 --> 00:01:35.900
Export handoff produces a readable plan for a colleague.

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:45.562
Later, after New plan, I open that saved JSON: teams, roles, pools, history, locked pick, comparisons, and notes return together.

00:01:47.562 --> 00:01:52.825
Open Reserve for free at blucca.github.io/series-reserve/.

00:01:52.845 --> 00:01:55.829
Files and calculations stay in your browser.

00:01:55.849 --> 00:01:57.584
Save before leaving.

00:01:57.604 --> 00:02:01.986
The source is MIT licensed, and every bundled example is fictional.

